    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n22946" root="شم" body-key="$">[
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مِشَمٌّ</span></b>  <i>An instrument of smelling;</i> like as <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مِسْمَعٌ</span>
signifies “ an instrument of hearing. ” ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  Hence,
its pl.] <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مَشَامُّ</span> signifies <i>Noses.</i> (KL.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b3-  [This pl.
is expl. by Jac. Schultens, as meaning <i>Perfumes</i>
(<i>odoramenta</i>): so says Freytag.]

